[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11296"] :question/problem "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={4}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =16+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =25 \\\\ R & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-80127/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "24f8d591-2c8d-573d-a01d-3527e59102a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80127/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer/id #uuid "6a8d7f8a-3c71-556b-8445-7aa7f3c7f447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80127/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "0619e003-ff41-52d7-9812-d1306996dc22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80127/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "56be5ad2-628d-58d3-8d53-104512895ae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80127/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "0656043c-f0c7-5b23-bee4-d9720cdf4921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80127/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26d4b70d-234a-5b4e-8578-70b92b1bc20d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80127/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-80127/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-80127/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" "q-80127/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-80127/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" "q-80127/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80127" :question/id #uuid "08e3efd6-39f9-56b1-8e11-679418895f9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80127" :question/problem "Given that the expression $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =9+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =25 \\\\ R & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80127/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dba0779-e903-5281-bc41-01b78c31a98c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80127"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327702/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "16ff5ae1-64d8-55a5-97fa-5ea6ed04364c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327702/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "cef0c156-0af1-5a35-afe8-010565294c2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327702/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f33140b1-86d5-5461-9ec1-b721fea76069" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327702/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-327702/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-327702/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327702" :question/id #uuid "5147ca83-8a3d-5ecb-8710-282192ad5618" :question/math-academy-id "q-327702" :question/problem "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+ϕ)$ with $R>0$, what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={4}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =16+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =25 \\\\ R & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-327702/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dba0779-e903-5281-bc41-01b78c31a98c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327702"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107555/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "d67ef0c7-cfb8-5e2e-a2e5-22b6bcc4c798" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107555/selection/4ef0fcc340e40ad6bcef1c832215cd28abf240aabeed43296dfece28d20d1935" :answer/id #uuid "559c1683-251a-5fee-bd02-09c7316f6e9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107555/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "aebfd566-b5db-5823-938c-2a630ec41af2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107555/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "25d7517b-02d7-5a40-8537-b21c82c16332" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107555/selection/5fd45cec95fc45f99550587cbe4d80dda358c751536fdf37920e2dff6de9568a" :answer/id #uuid "ce5d1eec-370e-53ce-a514-be7c682b5e13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107555/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "be30ef54-6a6a-556f-bd7c-c4ae25a85734" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107555/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-107555/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-107555/selection/4ef0fcc340e40ad6bcef1c832215cd28abf240aabeed43296dfece28d20d1935" "q-107555/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-107555/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-107555/selection/5fd45cec95fc45f99550587cbe4d80dda358c751536fdf37920e2dff6de9568a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107555" :question/id #uuid "15713217-5047-5f4b-8ba4-2a3e36222762" :question/math-academy-id "q-107555" :question/problem "Given that the expression $\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{5} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =5+4 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =9 \\\\ R & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107555/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3dba0779-e903-5281-bc41-01b78c31a98c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107555"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65582/selection/ec508878edfd1ac72232e580f5c036112ed6f0700297167c1140ceff806513c6" :answer/id #uuid "6b7dbb93-11c7-5278-a984-b75e31c9ca4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65582/selection/5454853a817db13094918bdbe0e10a99656ff85367ab90ccd985c0d49438056b" :answer/id #uuid "01b1e251-99af-519d-8f84-58d19d2c36a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65582/selection/bf31f50c9346bb27875cd964dc305f7f9c7b78104efc378f965ed284ca0752aa" :answer/id #uuid "ecb471e7-85b1-5c83-9cab-734d9c0a28aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65582/selection/a18cc11fa049f43e4fff538f471096d91a48bf133522de5f2be013b58e44141d" :answer/id #uuid "b77dd0b6-e1ea-5605-88bb-6fb938ff59f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65582/selection/1561acf2ee071f0d90b9e55c396cbf606ddad94050e0ef7511efcf5375286f0b" :answer/id #uuid "f31db222-f840-5886-aafa-4d2e070549fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65582/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0bba77f7-16a3-5aeb-a228-fc243a6f58eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65582/selection/5454853a817db13094918bdbe0e10a99656ff85367ab90ccd985c0d49438056b" :answer-field/choices ["q-65582/selection/ec508878edfd1ac72232e580f5c036112ed6f0700297167c1140ceff806513c6" "q-65582/selection/5454853a817db13094918bdbe0e10a99656ff85367ab90ccd985c0d49438056b" "q-65582/selection/bf31f50c9346bb27875cd964dc305f7f9c7b78104efc378f965ed284ca0752aa" "q-65582/selection/a18cc11fa049f43e4fff538f471096d91a48bf133522de5f2be013b58e44141d" "q-65582/selection/1561acf2ee071f0d90b9e55c396cbf606ddad94050e0ef7511efcf5375286f0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65582" :question/id #uuid "90b86949-70e2-5842-a82e-db95a00ca5eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-65582" :question/problem "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{10}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-65582/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65582"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107566/selection/90d094f7393e5d090cbc1f9cd42000bdd95cb31b3742b68d092926e6c124ff5c" :answer/id #uuid "91fed485-ac85-58d5-a02b-8198a1260444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107566/selection/3b28495977b1653d3b265084c301e2471a25911cfc996ab9fb4d1bd2f087ac51" :answer/id #uuid "1dc000fb-7997-5b05-8bc0-66fee55902fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107566/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" :answer/id #uuid "907fb84b-2bc2-5530-b0a4-2e17b6287e30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107566/selection/0ce4cdf24ea0065afc1ca1aa3662482333335a4ba13685e5f9035d4b2c16baef" :answer/id #uuid "0968df96-9af7-5455-8c52-0851f7b8e7e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107566/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer/id #uuid "c51c9d3f-6e82-56cf-a49b-fb5434df1b57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107566/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1594ce40-395f-5cb0-98ed-bd958a269d1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107566/selection/90d094f7393e5d090cbc1f9cd42000bdd95cb31b3742b68d092926e6c124ff5c" :answer-field/choices ["q-107566/selection/90d094f7393e5d090cbc1f9cd42000bdd95cb31b3742b68d092926e6c124ff5c" "q-107566/selection/3b28495977b1653d3b265084c301e2471a25911cfc996ab9fb4d1bd2f087ac51" "q-107566/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" "q-107566/selection/0ce4cdf24ea0065afc1ca1aa3662482333335a4ba13685e5f9035d4b2c16baef" "q-107566/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107566" :question/id #uuid "50a9ebe0-71cc-5992-ae58-512f2d215118" :question/math-academy-id "q-107566" :question/problem "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107566/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107566"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107571/selection/193085030deedd7dc5fe560427660b21855c3fc43a618f2597ddbe5ec35ee32c" :answer/id #uuid "cf8168b0-0a26-5616-9a54-aeb2ba97df5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{60}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107571/selection/7e6a777805130f4ecf0d6306d4ed25b5e9751f287e4316b33efa99a637131c17" :answer/id #uuid "8d18f2b5-ac62-53dc-8399-cf003c234260" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{60}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107571/selection/cf9b60b4876ad4879f6aea44cf212bb6a47a62dd255554fa654a915305441d16" :answer/id #uuid "3990a6ad-690b-54b4-a49e-18a9769bab10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{60}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107571/selection/cd72cdd56ca277c9babc217e8b3cbf0e866581f97034de98080387741e928332" :answer/id #uuid "2688dc9d-f91e-5b09-9089-45ba7755bfdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107571/selection/709106b91f4a75458e2368baacec8ba771eccaa7dc63f57021b155005b70c3bc" :answer/id #uuid "b50dc54e-5696-52e0-aecb-45bda389ceff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107571/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6e0514f-735b-5234-886e-bba0f0fab573" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107571/selection/709106b91f4a75458e2368baacec8ba771eccaa7dc63f57021b155005b70c3bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-107571/selection/193085030deedd7dc5fe560427660b21855c3fc43a618f2597ddbe5ec35ee32c" "q-107571/selection/7e6a777805130f4ecf0d6306d4ed25b5e9751f287e4316b33efa99a637131c17" "q-107571/selection/cf9b60b4876ad4879f6aea44cf212bb6a47a62dd255554fa654a915305441d16" "q-107571/selection/cd72cdd56ca277c9babc217e8b3cbf0e866581f97034de98080387741e928332" "q-107571/selection/709106b91f4a75458e2368baacec8ba771eccaa7dc63f57021b155005b70c3bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107571" :question/id #uuid "fe246caf-ce2b-52bd-a786-74626585ee11" :question/math-academy-id "q-107571" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{6} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\ ϕ & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{6})^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =6+2 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =8 \\\\ R & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107571/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107571"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11291/selection/cf45f0dabc72cf695aa0837275b622ca4e3ed87ed0dac1dc20cbb4eac3ba1e29" :answer/id #uuid "4e20f637-fb04-5811-a251-bf2a46b8c580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{41}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.896)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11291/selection/36addb4008bf0242672aea9c45cfed8bbb6dfb9b95003438aaedf4650833be18" :answer/id #uuid "2b37b80c-7523-5b79-a685-2b5230d8378c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{20}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.896)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11291/selection/44105979574e9862e954e9403aa074dbab6d633b8af42145432da0d7344a2db0" :answer/id #uuid "1e0067ac-71c0-55b1-9c88-3be58b65cea9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{40}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.968)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11291/selection/7573cc434c44b689fec376612f2f448a70c51dbe3498abfdbebfb4d99c736424" :answer/id #uuid "23d3f2a2-6175-5e6b-98fb-3dee85b7592c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.689)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11291/selection/726bd92b50bdeb9da7e3e130f7249ac844141874fdcd4b35e60a621c4b34fd05" :answer/id #uuid "b68690ab-39b4-5ec0-a87b-a3c61e9381a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{41}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.103)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11291/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a30d2232-7c02-5757-91ca-f86a0dcf8ab7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11291/selection/cf45f0dabc72cf695aa0837275b622ca4e3ed87ed0dac1dc20cbb4eac3ba1e29" :answer-field/choices ["q-11291/selection/cf45f0dabc72cf695aa0837275b622ca4e3ed87ed0dac1dc20cbb4eac3ba1e29" "q-11291/selection/36addb4008bf0242672aea9c45cfed8bbb6dfb9b95003438aaedf4650833be18" "q-11291/selection/44105979574e9862e954e9403aa074dbab6d633b8af42145432da0d7344a2db0" "q-11291/selection/7573cc434c44b689fec376612f2f448a70c51dbe3498abfdbebfb4d99c736424" "q-11291/selection/726bd92b50bdeb9da7e3e130f7249ac844141874fdcd4b35e60a621c4b34fd05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11291" :question/id #uuid "db5a83a4-ad24-5ad1-a438-4f752f0186b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-11291" :question/problem "$4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\  & ≈0.896\\,\\text{rad}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ & ={5}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =25+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =41 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{41}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$ \n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n \n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈\\sqrt{41}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.896)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11291/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11291"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327980/field-1/b79004dbe222c09b8b6840b3c412a7a19adf4f00d722dadcd375b60e4e6a5c2b" :answer/id #uuid "8f50bc66-e728-5185-a6ff-e2c78f9cf419" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{41}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327980/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f27cf1fa-5be8-598a-8a55-000615a29bdd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327980/field-1/b79004dbe222c09b8b6840b3c412a7a19adf4f00d722dadcd375b60e4e6a5c2b" :answer-field/choices ["q-327980/field-1/b79004dbe222c09b8b6840b3c412a7a19adf4f00d722dadcd375b60e4e6a5c2b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327980/field-2/2c38e90afbbdc10fe5dd7fd16266e19a6225768ecc67ff191ac8621b5a82a19f" :answer/id #uuid "121f5b62-7509-59b6-844c-10d987d22245" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.675" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327980/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "58182dcf-2261-57cd-a5cf-e3a3276baf22" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327980/field-2/2c38e90afbbdc10fe5dd7fd16266e19a6225768ecc67ff191ac8621b5a82a19f" :answer-field/choices ["q-327980/field-2/2c38e90afbbdc10fe5dd7fd16266e19a6225768ecc67ff191ac8621b5a82a19f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327980" :question/id #uuid "3f2fc169-ddc7-5649-97f0-be43b7857d67" :question/math-academy-id "q-327980" :question/problem "Express $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ in the form $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Use the **exact value** for $R,$ and round $ϕ$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n$5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{4}{5}) \\\\ ϕ & ≈0.675\\,\\text{rad},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡(ϕ)+{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡(ϕ) & ={4}^{2}+{5}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡(ϕ)+{cos}^{2}⁡(ϕ)) & =16+25 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =41 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{41}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)≈\\sqrt{41}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.675)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327980/field-1" "q-327980/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327980"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274609/field-1/438469ab2d71e1bb8b63f3164bacb1bbb54e29062b14dce6a666b63ac0081609" :answer/id #uuid "205445fb-23cb-5ea2-ba6a-d6bbde11cc46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186266596 :answer-field/choices ["q-274609/field-1/438469ab2d71e1bb8b63f3164bacb1bbb54e29062b14dce6a666b63ac0081609"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-30580"] :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ)\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =1+3 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =4 \\\\ R & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-30578/selection/abd6819ee2475928f5f773a6e7869462b5cae985b9333dcd6b4b62df23327972" :answer/id #uuid "bf539e6c-9683-5970-a6b8-76bd7812b4ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{45}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30578/selection/3379ee15fc7df2798bab271689b7bdcae54e417dd9025427c8ee445a0484919c" :answer/id #uuid "0b9dd3d0-35bf-5aa8-80c2-d3af0387b25c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{15}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30578/selection/6062b6c4335f5a71b5eef4a7a49a5f3f97a309351139bdfdec85565d6322da8f" :answer/id #uuid "ae7e98c2-c588-5ccf-93fc-57ee0075732c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{35}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30578/selection/c4d7c12a44b79cb451a4ef5357421a4f8131ea0cc3a8071b1ddef67d8b8df5a9" :answer/id #uuid "bfbe4b47-3978-5026-a327-9e5f70f75379" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30578/selection/436acf4828d3336d60746cd3369484525e0f3ee5d0ed633598c3dabf867bf0a2" :answer/id #uuid "9d0e9e15-d6aa-5793-b29c-a81a96fb60c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{45}^{∘})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30578/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa78be67-d613-58c8-97cf-414b4c45494e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-30578/selection/abd6819ee2475928f5f773a6e7869462b5cae985b9333dcd6b4b62df23327972" :answer-field/choices ["q-30578/selection/abd6819ee2475928f5f773a6e7869462b5cae985b9333dcd6b4b62df23327972" "q-30578/selection/3379ee15fc7df2798bab271689b7bdcae54e417dd9025427c8ee445a0484919c" "q-30578/selection/6062b6c4335f5a71b5eef4a7a49a5f3f97a309351139bdfdec85565d6322da8f" "q-30578/selection/c4d7c12a44b79cb451a4ef5357421a4f8131ea0cc3a8071b1ddef67d8b8df5a9" "q-30578/selection/436acf4828d3336d60746cd3369484525e0f3ee5d0ed633598c3dabf867bf0a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-30578" :question/id #uuid "4211d938-5e0f-5a8f-bb30-ab83971bd4ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-30578" :question/problem "$-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\ ϕ & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={4}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & ={4}^{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =32 \\\\ R & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{45}^{∘})\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-30578/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12d8028-2520-5706-ba49-d67935036af6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-30578"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3542"] :question/problem "Given that the expression $\\sqrt{2}\\sin x + \\sqrt{7}\\cos x$ can be written as $R\\sin(x+\\phi)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\sin x + \\sqrt{7}\\cos x   = R\\sin(x+\\phi),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\sin x + \\sqrt{7}\\cos x    = (R \\cos \\phi ) \\sin x + (R \\sin \\phi ) \\cos x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x,$ we have the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={\\sqrt{2}}^{2}+{\\sqrt{7}}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =2+7 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =9 \\\\ R & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3541"] :question/problem "Given that the expression $2\\sin{x}-2\\cos{x}$ can be written as $R\\sin(x-\\phi)$ with $0^\\circ  <       \\phi <        90^\\circ$ and $R>0,$ what is the value of $\\phi?$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2 \\sin x - 2 \\cos x = R\\sin(x-\\phi),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2 \\sin x - 2 \\cos x   = (R \\cos \\phi ) \\sin x - (R \\sin \\phi ) \\cos x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\  & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3543"] :question/problem "Write $3\\sin x-2\\cos x$ in the form $R\\sin(x-\\phi)$ with $\\phi \\in \\left( 0, \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\right)$. Round $\\phi$ to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3 \\sin x - 2 \\cos x    = R\\sin(x-\\phi) ,\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3 \\sin x - 2 \\cos x   = (R \\cos \\phi ) \\sin x - (R \\sin \\phi )\\cos x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & ≈0.588\\,\\text{rad}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(3)^{2}+(2)^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =9+4 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =13 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only considered the positive root, since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\sin(x)-2\\cos(x) \\approx \\sqrt{13} \\sin \\left(x - 0.588 \\right)\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3544"] :question/problem "Write $3\\cos x - \\sqrt{3}\\sin x$ in the form $R\\cos(x+\\phi)$ with $\\phi \\in \\left( 0, \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\right).$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3\\cos x - \\sqrt{3}\\sin x   = R\\cos(x+\\phi)\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3\\cos x - \\sqrt{3}\\sin x   = (R \\cos \\phi) \\cos x -( R \\sin \\phi )\\sin x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={3}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =9+3 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =12 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\cos x - \\sqrt{3}\\sin x = 2\\sqrt{3}\\cos\\left(x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
